 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut the soft <b>kombu</b> left from making dashi into thin strips, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">3 cm</span> long.</li><li>Simmer with the <b>water</b>, <b>soy</b>, <b>sugar</b>, <b>mirin</b> and <b>vinegar</b> over low heat, stirring now and then, until the liquid is gone and the kombu is glossy, <b>15–20 minutes</b>.</li><li>Off the heat, stir in the <b>shiso</b>, cut into fine strips. See the keeping note below.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
